    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d722">

                <pb facs="0909" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg901"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits/4362: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-13T14:00:00+09:00">November 13,
                            1941—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 22—1:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1795. On November 11, 1941, the Japanese Government published in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Official Gazette</hi> general licenses Nos. 61 and 62 of
                    the Ministry of Finance which in effect unfreeze American Government
                    establishments and personnel in Japan.</p>
                <p>[Here follow texts of translations of the general licenses.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
